# Dwell & head-mouse accessibility

Chase drives every app with a **gyro head-mounted mouse + dwell click**. There is
no "just click it" fallback and no "hold perfectly still" either.

## 🔴 Read this before writing hover / dwell / drag code

**`cursor-patterns/dwell-and-head-mouse.md`**

That file is the **single source of truth**. It holds every timing value, the four
existing implementations and why they legitimately differ, the "grep before you
build" index, the non-negotiable behaviors, and the anti-patterns.

**This rule deliberately contains no numbers.** Timings and thresholds live in
that one file so they cannot drift out of sync across copies. If you need a
value, open it — do not guess, and do not copy a number from any other doc.

## The two rules that subsume the rest

1. **Every hover affordance must also have a click path.** Chase cannot rely on
   precise hover.
2. **Assume every hovered element gets clicked.** The toolbar fires a real
   OS-level click on whatever the cursor rests on. Design so that click is
   harmless, or is the intended action.

## Before you build anything hover/dwell/drag-shaped

Several implementations already exist (hooks, latch utilities, overlay poll
hubs). Adding another is a **stop-and-surface**, not a judgment call — see
§ *Grep before you build* in the source-of-truth file for the index of what to
reuse and its exemplar consumer.

Exemplar rule to copy the *shape* of:
`School Scrips/Math App Studio/.cursor/rules/studio-dwell-mechanics.mdc`
